 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-- **Boundary Checks**: The `is_solid` function must explicitly handle chunk boundaries by returning false for out-of-bounds coordinates, treating out-of-bounds space as air [S3, S4, unofficial]. Failure to do so results in missing faces at chunk edges.
-- **Precision**: Floating-point precision issues may arise when calculating vertex positions if chunk offsets are large. Using integer arithmetic for block coordinates and converting to float only for vertex positions is recommended.
+- **Boundary Checks**: The `is_solid` function must explicitly handle chunk boundaries by returning false for out-of-bounds coordinates, treating out-of-bounds space as air [S3, S4, unofficial]. Failure to do so results in missing faces at chunk edges [S3, S4, unofficial].
+- **Precision**: Floating-point precision issues may arise when calculating vertex positions if chunk offsets are large. Using integer arithmetic for block coordinates and converting to float only for vertex positions is recommended [G].
 - **Transparent Blocks**: Transparent blocks (e.g., glass) require special handling. They may need to be rendered in a separate pass with depth sorting to avoid z-fighting or incorrect transparency blending [S2, S3, unofficial].
 
