 ## Background
 
-Voxel Mesh Generation with Face Culling is a foundational technique in voxel-based game development, originating from early Minecraft clones and sandbox games. It was popularized by the need to render large voxel worlds efficiently on limited hardware. The method is widely used in educational voxel engines and indie games due to its simplicity and effectiveness. Key implementations include [exolands](https://github.com/kvxy/exolands) [S2, unofficial], [voxel-compare](https://github.com/scarlyle0/voxel-compare) [S3, unofficial], and [voxel-engine](https://github.com/ernerdgn/voxel-engine) [S4, unofficial]. The technique has evolved to include optimizations such as baked lighting, texture atlases, and transparent block sorting [S2, S3, S4, unofficial].
